            <ArticleTitle>Autoimmune and inflammatory responses may have an additive effect in postpercutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients who had an increase in their serum amyloid type A level of &gt; 100% in the first 24 hours after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) and also developed a positive antibody result (antinuclear factor or anticardiolipin), had a relative risk of 10.6 for developing restenosis in the first year after PTCA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
